<body>
<div class="container">

<header>
  <h1>American Express (AXP) Historical Stock Performance Report</h1>
  <p>Comprehensive analysis of over 50 years of daily trading data (1972–2026) for investor decision-making.</p>
  <div class="meta">
    <span>Data: 13,556 trading days</span>
    <span>Period: June 1972 – March 2026</span>
    <span>Source: AXP Adjusted Daily OHLCV</span>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- KPI Dashboard -->
<div class="kpi-grid" id="kpi-dashboard"></div>

<!-- Executive Overview -->
<section id="executive-overview">
  <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
  <p>American Express has delivered one of the most remarkable long-term wealth-creation stories in U.S. financial services. From an adjusted price of <strong>$1.22</strong> in June 1972 to <strong>$305.99</strong> in March 2026, the stock generated a cumulative capital appreciation of <strong>24,895%</strong> — equivalent to a compounded annual growth rate (CAGR) of <strong>10.81%</strong> over 53.8 years.</p>
  <p>However, this return came with significant volatility. The stock experienced a maximum drawdown of <strong>−83.9%</strong> during the 2008 Global Financial Crisis, and annualized volatility sits at <strong>34.69%</strong> — well above the S&P 500 long-term average. Investors who held through the crises were rewarded, but the journey required substantial risk tolerance.</p>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> AXP has been a high-return, high-volatility equity. Its 10.81% CAGR over five decades outperforms broad market averages, but drawdowns exceeding 40% have occurred in every major economic crisis. Dividends contributed $34.27 per share cumulatively, with yield declining from ~6.8% in the 1980s to ~1.1% in the 2020s as price appreciation outpaced payout growth.
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Long-Term Price Trend Analysis -->
<section id="price-trend-analysis">
  <h2>Long-Term Price Trend Analysis</h2>
  <p>The closing price trajectory reveals six distinct macro regimes: the 1970s stagnation, the 1980s–1990s secular bull, the 2000s lost decade, the post-GFC recovery, the COVID shock, and the 2021–2025 expansion to all-time highs.</p>
  <div class="chart-container tall">
    <canvas id="priceChart"></canvas>
  </div>
  <p><strong>Bull & Bear Phases Identified:</strong></p>
  <div class="timeline" id="phases-timeline"></div>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <p><strong>CAGR by Sub-Period</strong></p>
      <table id="cagr-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Period</th><th>CAGR</th><th>Start → End</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p><strong>All-Time Highs & Lows</strong></p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Date</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>All-Time High</td><td>2025-02-14</td><td>$384.04</td></tr>
          <tr><td>All-Time Low</td><td>1974-10-03</td><td>$0.38</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Pre-GFC Peak</td><td>2007-07-19</td><td>$49.30</td></tr>
          <tr><td>GFC Trough</td><td>2009-03-06</td><td>$7.93</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Pre-COVID Peak</td><td>2020-02-24</td><td>$126.63</td></tr>
          <tr><td>COVID Trough</td><td>2020-03-23</td><td>$63.77</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Volatility & Risk Assessment -->
<section id="volatility-risk">
  <h2>Volatility & Risk Assessment</h2>
  <p>AXP's annualized volatility of 34.69% reflects its sensitivity to credit cycles, consumer spending, and financial system stress. The stock exhibits pronounced tail risk — extreme negative returns cluster around systemic crises.</p>
  <div class="chart-container">
    <canvas id="drawdownChart"></canvas>
  </div>
  <p><strong>Worst Drawdown Episodes (Quantified)</strong></p>
  <table id="drawdown-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Episode</th><th>Peak Date</th><th>Trough Date</th><th>Drawdown</th><th>Recovery</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody></tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:20px;">
    <div class="chart-container wide">
      <canvas id="volatilityChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-container wide">
      <canvas id="annualReturnChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Trading Volume Analysis -->
<section id="volume-analysis">
  <h2>Trading Volume Analysis</h2>
  <p>Volume data becomes reliable after the early 1970s (zero-volume records in 181 early rows). Structural shifts in liquidity are visible: the 1980s–1990s averaged ~2.6M shares/day, while the 2000s–2010s saw a step-up to ~5.5M shares/day, reflecting electronic trading and ETF inclusion.</p>
  <div class="chart-container">
    <canvas id="volumeChart"></canvas>
  </div>
  <p><strong>Volume Spikes & Correlation with Events</strong></p>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    The single highest volume day was <strong>April 24, 2009</strong> (90.3M shares), coinciding with a +20.6% price surge during the GFC recovery. Other major spikes clustered in 2008–2009 (Lehman aftermath, TARP uncertainty) and October 1984 (63.6M shares, likely split-related rebalancing).
  </div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Decade</th><th>Avg Daily Volume</th><th>Max Single-Day Volume</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody id="volume-table-body"></tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<!-- Dividend History & Stock Splits -->
<section id="dividends-splits">
  <h2>Dividend History & Stock Splits</h2>
  <p>AXP has paid dividends consistently since at least 1977, with 197 recorded distribution events totaling <strong>$34.27 per share</strong>. The dividend yield peaked in the high-interest-rate 1980s (~6.8% average) and has compressed to ~1.1% in the 2020s as share price appreciation outpaced payout growth.</p>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="chart-container wide">
      <canvas id="dividendChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-container wide">
      <canvas id="yieldChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p><strong>Stock Splits</strong></p>
  <table id="splits-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Split Ratio</th><th>Price at Split</th><th>Cumulative Factor</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody></tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Income Investor Note:</strong> While absolute dividend dollars grew from ~$0.02/share quarterly in 1977 to ~$0.80/share quarterly in 2025, the yield on cost for a 1972 buyer is extraordinary. A $1.22 initial investment now generates ~$2.60/year in dividends alone — a <strong>~213% yield on original cost</strong>.
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Decade-by-Decade Performance Comparison -->
<section id="decade-comparison">
  <h2>Decade-by-Decade Performance Comparison</h2>
  <p>Comparing AXP across decades reveals how macroeconomic regimes shaped returns. The 1980s and 1990s were the golden era (20%+ CAGR each), while the 2000s delivered essentially zero price appreciation despite high volatility.</p>
  <div class="chart-container">
    <canvas id="decadeChart"></canvas>
  </div>
  <table id="decade-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Decade</th><th>Start Price</th><th>End Price</th><th>Total Return</th><th>CAGR</th><th>Volatility</th><th>Dividends</th><th>Price Range</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody></tbody>
  </table>
  <p style="margin-top:18px;"><strong>Monthly Return Heatmap (Annual View)</strong></p>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
    <div id="heatmap-container"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer>
  Report generated from AXP daily stock data (1972–2026). All figures computed directly from dataset. Past performance does not guarantee future results.
</footer>

</div>

<script>
// Load data
fetch('data.json')
  .then(r => r.json())
  .then(data => {
    renderKPIs(data.kpis);
    renderPriceChart(data.price);
    renderPhases(data.price);
    renderCAGRTable(data.price);
    renderDrawdownChart(data.drawdown);
    renderDrawdownTable(data.episodes);
    renderVolatilityChart(data.annual);
    renderAnnualReturnChart(data.annual);
    renderVolumeChart(data.price);
    renderVolumeTable(data.volume_decade, data.price);
    renderDividendChart(data.dividends);
    renderYieldChart(data.dividends);
    renderSplitsTable(data.splits);
    renderDecadeChart(data.decade);
    renderDecadeTable(data.decade);
    renderHeatmap(data.monthly);
  });

function renderKPIs(kpis) {
  const items = [
    { label: 'Cumulative Return', value: '+' + kpis.cumulative_return_pct.toLocaleString() + '%', cls: 'positive', sub: '$' + kpis.start_price + ' → $' + kpis.end_price },
    { label: 'CAGR (53.8 Yrs)', value: '+' + kpis.cagr_pct + '%', cls: 'positive', sub: 'Annualized growth' },
    { label: 'Max Drawdown', value: kpis.max_drawdown_pct + '%', cls: 'negative', sub: 'Worst peak-to-trough' },
    { label: 'Annualized Volatility', value: kpis.annualized_volatility_pct + '%', cls: 'neutral', sub: 'Daily returns × √252' },
    { label: 'Total Dividends', value: '$' + kpis.total_dividends, cls: 'positive', sub: 'Per share cumulative' },
    { label: 'Sharpe-like Ratio', value: kpis.sharpe_like, cls: 'neutral', sub: 'CAGR / Volatility' }
  ];
  document.getElementById('kpi-dashboard').innerHTML = items.map(i => `
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">${i.label}</div>
      <div class="kpi-value ${i.cls}">${i.value}</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">${i.sub}</div>
    </div>
  `).join('');
}

function renderPriceChart(price) {
  const ctx = document.getElementById('priceChart').getContext('2d');
  const labels = price.map(d => d.Date);
  const closes = price.map(d => d.Close);
  new Chart(ctx, {
    type: 'line',
    data: {
      labels,
      datasets: [{
        label: 'Close Price (Adj)',
        data: closes,
        borderColor: '#3b82f6',
        backgroundColor: 'rgba(59,130,246,0.08)',
        fill: true,
        pointRadius: 0,
        borderWidth: 1.5,
        tension: 0.1
      }]
    },
    options: {
      responsive: true,
      maintainAspectRatio: false,
      interaction: { mode: 'index', intersect: false },
      plugins: {
        legend: { display: false },
        tooltip: {
          callbacks: { label: c => '$' + c.parsed.y.toFixed(2) }
        }
      },
      scales: {
        x: { ticks: { maxTicksLimit: 10, color: '#94a3b8' }, grid: { color: '#334155' } },
        y: { ticks: { color: '#94a3b8' }, grid: { color: '#334155' }, type: 'log' }
      }
    }
  });
}

function renderPhases(price) {
  const phases = [
    { date: '1972-06-01', label: 'IPO Era Start', price: 1.22 },
    { date: '1973-01-24', label: 'Oil Crisis Peak', price: 1.40 },
    { date: '1974-10-03', label: 'Oil Crisis Trough', price: 0.38 },
    { date: '1987-08-25', label: 'Pre-Black Monday', price: 5.00 },
    { date: '1987-12-03', label: 'Post-Crash Trough', price: 2.77 },
    { date: '1990-10-17', label: 'Gulf War Trough', price: 2.52 },
    { date: '2000-11-08', label: 'Dot-Com Peak', price: 35.90 },
    { date: '2001-09-21', label: 'Post-9/11 Trough', price: 15.94 },
    { date: '2007-07-19', label: 'Pre-GFC Peak', price: 49.30 },
    { date: '2009-03-06', label: 'GFC Trough', price: 7.93 },
    { date: '2020-02-24', label: 'Pre-COVID Peak', price: 118.54 },
    { date: '2020-03-23', label: 'COVID Trough', price: 63.77 },
    { date: '2025-02-14', label: 'All-Time High', price: 384.04 },
    { date: '2026-03-11', label: 'Latest Close', price: 305.99 }
  ];
  document.getElementById('phases-timeline').innerHTML = phases.map((p, i) => {
    const prev = i > 0 ? phases[i-1] : null;
    const change = prev ? ((p.price - prev.price)/prev.price*100).toFixed(1) : null;
    const cls = change > 0 ? 'positive' : 'negative';
    return `<div class="timeline-item">
      <div class="timeline-date">${p.date}</div>
      <div class="timeline-body">${p.label} — $${p.price.toFixed(2)}</div>
      ${change !== null ? `<div class="timeline-pct ${cls}">${change>0?'+':''}${change}%</div>` : '<div class="timeline-pct">—</div>'}
    </div>`;
  }).join('');
}

function renderCAGRTable(price) {
  const periods = [
    { name: 'Full Period', start: '1972-06-01', end: '2026-03-11' },
    { name: '1970s', start: '1972-06-01', end: '1979-12-31' },
    { name: '1980s', start: '1980-01-01', end: '1989-12-31' },
    { name: '1990s', start: '1990-01-01', end: '1999-12-31' },
    { name: '2000s', start: '2000-01-01', end: '2009-12-31' },
    { name: '2010s', start: '2010-01-01', end: '2019-12-31' },
    { name: '2020s*', start: '2020-01-01', end: '2026-03-11' },
    { name: 'Post-GFC', start: '2009-03-06', end: '2026-03-11' },
    { name: 'Post-COVID', start: '2020-03-23', end: '2026-03-11' }
  ];
  const tbody = document.querySelector('#cagr-table tbody');
  tbody.innerHTML = periods.map(p => {
    const startRow = price.find(r => r.Date >= p.start);
    const endRow = price.slice().reverse().find(r => r.Date <= p.end);
    if (!startRow || !endRow) return '';
    const years = (new Date(endRow.Date) - new Date(startRow.Date)) / (365.25*24*3600*1000);
    const cagr = ((endRow.Close / startRow.Close) ** (1/Math.max(years, 0.1)) - 1) * 100;
    const cls = cagr >= 0 ? 'positive' : 'negative';
    return `<tr><td>${p.name}</td><td class="${cls}">${cagr.toFixed(1)}%</td><td>$${startRow.Close.toFixed(2)} → $${endRow.Close.toFixed(2)}</td></tr>`;
  }).join('');
}

function renderDrawdownChart(drawdown) {
  const ctx = document.getElementById('drawdownChart').getContext('2d');
  new Chart(ctx, {
    type: 'line',
    data: {
      labels: drawdown.map(d => d.Date),
      datasets: [{
        label: 'Drawdown %',
        data: drawdown.map(d => d.Drawdown),
        borderColor: '#ef4444',
        backgroundColor: 'rgba(239,68,68,0.15)',
        fill: true,
        pointRadius: 0,
        borderWidth: 1
      }]
    },
    options: {
      responsive: true,
      maintainAspectRatio: false,
      plugins: { legend: { display: false } },
      scales: {
        x: { ticks: { maxTicksLimit: 10, color: '#94a3b8' }, grid: { color: '#334155' } },
        y: { ticks: { color: '#94a3b8' }, grid: { color: '#334155' } }
      }
    }
  });
}

function renderDrawdownTable(episodes) {
  const tbody = document.querySelector('#drawdown-table tbody');
  tbody.innerHTML = episodes.map(ep => {
    const rec = ep.recovery_date ? ep.recovery_date : 'Not recovered';
    return `<tr>
      <td style="text-align:left">${ep.peak_date} → ${ep.trough_date}</td>
      <td>$${ep.peak_price}</td>
      <td>$${ep.trough_price}</td>
      <td class="negative">${ep.drawdown}%</td>
      <td>${rec}</td>
      <td>${ep.duration_days} days</td>
    </tr>`;
  }).join('');
}

function renderVolatilityChart(annual) {
  const ctx = document.getElementById('volatilityChart').getContext('2d');
  new Chart(ctx, {
    type: 'bar',
    data: {
      labels: annual.map(d => d.Year),
      datasets: [{
        label: 'Annualized Volatility %',
        data: annual.map(d => d.volatility),
        backgroundColor: annual.map(d => d.volatility > 40 ? '#ef4444' : '#3b82f6'),
        borderRadius: 3
      }]
    },
    options: {
      responsive: true,
      maintainAspectRatio: false,
      plugins: { legend: { display: false }, title: { display: true, text: 'Annual Volatility', color: '#f1f5f9' } },
      scales: {
        x: { ticks: { maxTicksLimit: 10, color: '#94a3b8' }, grid: { color: '#334155' } },
        y: { ticks: { color: '#94a3b8' }, grid: { color: '#334155' } }
      }
    }
  });
}

function renderAnnualReturnChart(annual) {
  const ctx = document.getElementById('annualReturnChart').getContext('2d');
  new Chart(ctx, {
    type: 'bar',
    data: {
      labels: annual.map(d => d.Year),
      datasets: [{
        label: 'Annual Return %',
        data: annual.map(d => d.return),
        backgroundColor: annual.map(d => d.return >= 0 ? '#22c55e' : '#ef4444'),
        borderRadius: 3
      }]
    },
    options: {
      responsive: true,
      maintainAspectRatio: false,
      plugins: { legend: { display: false }, title: { display: true, text: 'Annual Returns', color: '#f1f5f9' } },
      scales: {
        x: { ticks: { maxTicksLimit: 10, color: '#94a3b8' }, grid: { color: '#334155' } },
        y: { ticks: { color: '#94a3b8' }, grid: { color: '#334155' } }
      }
    }
  });
}

function renderVolumeChart(price) {
  const ctx = document.getElementById('volumeChart').getContext('2d');
  const volData = price.filter(d => d.Volume > 0);
  // Downsample for performance
  const sampled = volData.filter((_, i) => i % 5 === 0);
  new Chart(ctx, {
    type: 'line',
    data: {
      labels: sampled.map(d => d.Date),
      datasets: [{
        label: 'Volume',
        data: sampled.map(d => d.Volume),
        borderColor: '#f59e0b',
        backgroundColor: 'rgba(245,158,11,0.08)',
        fill: true,
        pointRadius: 0,
        borderWidth: 1
      }]
    },
    options: {
      responsive: true,
      maintainAspectRatio: false,
      plugins: { legend: { display: false } },
      scales: {
        x: { ticks: { maxTicksLimit: 10, color: '#94a3b8' }, grid: { color: '#334155' } },
        y: { ticks: { color: '#94a3b8', callback: v => (v/1e6).toFixed(0)+'M' }, grid: { color: '#334155' } }
      }
    }
  });
}

function renderVolumeTable(volDecade, price) {
  const tbody = document.getElementById('volume-table-body');
  const decades = [1970, 1980, 1990, 2000, 2010, 2020];
  tbody.innerHTML = decades.map(dec => {
    const vd = volDecade.find(v => v.Decade === dec);
    const decPrice = price.filter(p => {
      const y = parseInt(p.Date.split('-')[0]);
      return y >= dec && y < dec+10 && p.Volume > 0;
    });
    const maxVol = decPrice.length ? Math.max(...decPrice.map(p => p.Volume)) : 0;
    return `<tr><td>${dec}s</td><td>${vd ? (vd.avg_volume/1e6).toFixed(1)+'M' : 'N/A'}</td><td>${maxVol ? (maxVol/1e6).toFixed(1)+'M' : 'N/A'}</td></tr>`;
  }).join('');
}

